            "dct:references": "https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1097-0185(199804)253:2<49::AID-AR8>3.0.CO;2-9",
            "dct:title": "3D Reference Organ for Skin, Female",
            "rdfs:comment": "This reference organ, Skin-female (https://humanatlas.io/3d-reference-library) was created using data from the Visible\nHuman Dataset, provided by the National Library of Medicine (Spitzer and Whitlock 2002). In version v1.3, the torso of\nthe skin model was moved up from previous editions to incorporate the clavicles and other anatomy for the breast. It\nwas also adjusted to add space for the triceps surae and the ankle bones for the eventual addition of the triceps\nsurae muscles and landmark organs. In v2.3, the head was adjusted to be more like the original skin of the Visible\nHuman Female, to make space for the mouth 3D object and landmarks.\n\n**Bibliography:**\n\n* Spitzer, Victor M., and David G. Whitlock. 2002. “The Visible Human Dataset: The Anatomical Platform for Human Simulation.” *The Anatomical Record* 253 (2): 49–57. https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1097-0185(199804)253:2<49::AID-AR8>3.0.CO;2-9.",
